# CoW view-materialization on the GENERIC FREE FUNCTION body-lowering path.
#
# AXIS CELL — path = `lower_generic_function` (src/ir/lowering/functions.rs).
# One of eleven function-body-lowering paths; the five per-function CoW /
# auto-move prescans used to be hand-copied into only two of them, so this one
# lowered with an EMPTY `cow_reassigned_after`: `is_source_mut_unsafe_at`
# answered false, the element view stayed a lazy borrow, and the 64 pushes
# reallocated the buffer out from under it.
#
# THE REALLOC IS LOAD-BEARING (64 pushes; one push is rc 0 and proves nothing),
# and the payload is heap-FORCED via `mk` so the freed element is a heap String
# and ASan reports a legible heap-use-after-free rather than a bare SIGSEGV.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix compiler: rc 139 SIGSEGV on C AND LLVM.
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS FIXTURE IS IN A SUBDIRECTORY AND NOT AT TOP LEVEL. Every top-level
# `tests/fixtures/*.gg` is auto-scanned into `runtime_parity_corpus`, and this
# program does not MATCH on the self-host lane — for a reason that has nothing
# to do with the cell it tests (see the `#[ignore]`d self-host test wired
# alongside it). Core #9 ⊕ forbids raising `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING` for a
# round's OWN inflow, so the fixture stays out of the auto-scanned set. It is
# STILL a live regression guard: `run_gg` runs it on C and on LLVM, and
# `tests/fixtures/security/` symlinks it for the ASan lane. Only the parity
# corpus is opted out of, and only until the self-host defect is fixed.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

T probe[T](Vector[T] &v, T x):
    T s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(x)
        i = i + 1
    return s

void main():
    Vector[String] v = [mk("hello", "world")]
    print(probe(&v, mk("xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx", "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy")))
